==French==
{{wikipedia|lang=fr}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|fr|chabbat}}, {{l|fr|shabbat}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{term|sabbata|lang=la}} or {{term|sabbatum|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|fr}} {{term|σάββατον||Sabbath|lang=grc}}, from {{etyl|he|fr}} {{term|שבת||Sabbath|lang=he|tr=shabát}}.<br>In regards to the semantic evolution to "witches' meeting" compare with {{term|ramdam|lang=fr}}, {{term|brouhaha|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sa.ba/|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# [[Sabbath]], biblical seventh day
#: ''Les juifs observent fort exactement le '''sabbat'''.''
# [[witches' Sabbath]], meeting of witches at midnight
#: ''Qu’est-ce que vous portez donc là, mon petit fieu ? — Des crapauds qui t’ont vue au '''sabbat''', vieille sorcière, répondit celui-ci.'' (Charles Deulin, Manneken-Pis)
# noisy [[meeting]]
#: ''Ces ivrognes ont fait un terrible '''sabbat'''.''

